# Overtime — Fair Labor Standards Act

> Module Overtime_flsa

Source: REAL-007, 29 U.S.C. § 207(a)(1), fetched verbatim from Cornell LII.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope Overtime:
  input hours_worked_in_week content decimal
  input regular_rate content money

  internal overtime_hours content decimal

  output overtime_pay content money
  output total_pay content money
```

## REAL-007, 29 U.S.C. § 207(a)(1)

  no employer shall employ any of his employees … for a workweek longer than forty hours
  unless such employee receives compensation for his employment in excess of the hours
  above specified at a rate not less than one and one-half times the regular rate at which
  he is employed.

```catala
scope Overtime:
  definition overtime_hours equals
    if hours_worked_in_week > 40.0 then hours_worked_in_week - 40.0 else 0.0

  definition overtime_pay equals regular_rate * overtime_hours * 1.5

  definition total_pay equals
    regular_rate * (if hours_worked_in_week > 40.0 then 40.0 else hours_worked_in_week)
    + overtime_pay
```
